{
  "title": "Pilot accepts stale tool calls after timeout recovery",
  "description": "In game_20260326_192635_g1, Grok4 Story timed out twice, \
the pilot advanced the game with timeout recovery, and then late completions \
from the timed-out prompts were still executed against the new decision state.\
\n\
\n\
Evidence:\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_pilot.log:160-165 \
shows a timeout at 19:52:50, then a late choose_action(choice=\"p35\") at \
19:54:44 failing with `Object p35 not found in current choices`.\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_llm_trace.jsonl:34 \
shows that very late response was grounded in an older Turn 3 precombat-main \
prompt where `p35` was still a legal land-drop choice.\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_llm.jsonl:77 shows \
the stale `p35` tool call hit game_seq 107, where the current choices were \
attacker IDs (`p24`, `p23`, `all`) rather than main-phase plays.\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_pilot.log:266-271 \
shows the same pattern again: timeout at 20:06:48, then a late \
choose_action(choice=\"p49\") at 20:07:53 failing with `Object p49 not found \
in current choices`.\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_llm_trace.jsonl:56 \
shows that late response came from an older Turn 4 precombat-main prompt \
where `p49` (`Welding Sparks`) was still a legal cast.\
\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_192635_g1/Grok4 Story_llm.jsonl:128 shows \
the stale `p49` tool call landed at game_seq 189, after timeout recovery had \
already advanced to attacker selection.\
\n\
\n\
Source:\
\n\
- src/magebench/pilot/pilot.py:554 wraps the LLM call in `asyncio.wait_for(...)`.\
\n\
- src/magebench/pilot/pilot_recovery.py:150-164 handles the timeout by \
immediately calling `pass_priority`, which advances the pending decision.\
\n\
\n\
Root cause:\
\n\
The timeout path advances the game state but does not fence off or discard the \
completion from the timed-out request. If the provider/client delivers that \
completion later, the pilot still processes its tool call even though the \
decision context has changed.\
\n\
\n\
Suggested fix:\
\n\
Track an LLM request generation / decision generation and ignore any response \
that is no longer current after timeout recovery, or otherwise guarantee the \
timed-out request cannot deliver tool calls after `_handle_timeout()` advances \
the game.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": ["pilot"],
